| phase-73 | `DONE` | B2-UI-3 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-73/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-UI-3 row). The shared `NoteRepository.lastSavedStrokeHash` diff cache + overlapping debounce/dispose-flush serialization: `lastSavedStrokeHash` (`NoteRepository.kt:911-912`) was a plain access-order `LruBoundedMap` mutated from both the load path (`getStrokesForPage`, no transaction) and the save path (`saveStrokesForPage`, inside `withTransaction`) on different coroutines with no locking — two concurrent same-page saves could interleave the read-modify-write (older hash commit lands last ⇒ newer stroke silently not inserted), interleave the two `withTransaction` delete+upsert rounds (dropped rows), or corrupt the map (`ConcurrentModificationException`). Fix: the map is now `Collections.synchronizedMap(LruBoundedMap<…>)` (per-op atomic, B2-DOS-10 LRU bound preserved) and a new `private val pageSaveLocks = ConcurrentHashMap<String, Mutex>()` (`:944`) gives each page ONE fair/FIFO kotlinx `Mutex` that `saveStrokesForPage` (`:986-988`), `saveMediaEmbedsForPage` (`:1165-1167`) and `saveLayersForPage` (`:1244-1246`) ALL acquire via `lock.withLock { db.withTransaction { … } }` — the full strokes→embeds→layers snapshot is atomic per page, different pages stay concurrent, and a later-issued (newer) save commits last. `EditorScreen.kt:443-451` dispose now captures the pending debounce `saveJob`, nulls it, and routes through the new `NoteflowViewModel.disposeEditorPageFlush` (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:2875-2892`) which `cancel()`s the stale debounce → `join()`s any already-started write → flushes the FINAL newest snapshot; `autosaveStrokes` (`:2907-2920`) is `suspend fun` running the write inline in the debounce job so it is cancellable/awaitable. `MarkdownBodySaveCoordinator`'s coroutine-Mutex precedent reused; no new deps (stdlib/JDK + kotlinx Mutex already in tree). No OS-floor issue (API-agnostic primitives). Tests: new `B2Ui3StrokeSaveConcurrencyTest` (11 — a pure-JVM behavioral model driven by the SAME `synchronizedMap` + per-page-`Mutex` primitives: concurrent RMW never throws/loses/duplicates entries and never exceeds the cap, newer full snapshot always commits after an in-flight older one, no delete+upsert interleave, different pages not serialized, dispose cancels a pending debounce / awaits an in-flight one / no-pending flush, + source-level wiring pins for repository locks, EditorScreen dispose, and the VM helper). `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` 1447 total (0 failures / 0 errors) + `gradle :app:assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |

| phase-74 | `DONE` | B2-UI-5 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-74/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-UI-5 row). Markdown note-body saves + reads are serialized and latest-wins (the last non-atomic body path — dispose-flush `File.writeText` vs `produceState` `File.readText` truncate-race — is gone; bodies live only in the field-encrypted `pages.extractedText` column). New pure-JVM `services/MarkdownBodySaveCoordinator.kt`: every body write serialized through a per-page `kotlinx.coroutines.Mutex`, monotonic `seq` stamped at `issue(...)` time, `commitLatest` refuses (never runs the write; settles so awaiters release) any request no longer the latest issued one — latest-wins is issue-ORDER, never time-based, so touching a page before a slow write can never let a stale snapshot win; the deferred-body unlock flush re-`issue`s on the calling thread BEFORE any write (strictly older than a new edit); `awaitSettled(pageId)` bounded by `SETTLE_AWAIT_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000L` and chases any request issued while a reader waits. `NoteflowViewModel.saveMarkdownNoteBody` (`NoteflowViewModel.kt:2214-2278`) issues on the UI thread then `commitLatest { repository.updatePageBody(...); NoteBodyVaultPolicy.deleteLegacyNoteTextBody(...importsDir) }` on `Dispatchers.IO`; the new `readMarkdownNoteBody` (`:2291-2336`) awaits settle + RE-FETCHES `repository.getPageById` (never a stale flow snapshot; deflates to the composition's in-memory snapshot only on a transient decrypt failure, so a key-lost race can never surface as an empty editor that gets saved over the real body); `flushPendingEditorSaves` (`:2929-2988`) drains via issue→commitLatest. Both markdown `produceState` blocks (`MainActivity.kt:438/536`) read `viewModel.readMarkdownNoteBody(page.id, page.extractedText, page.sourceFilePath, page.sourceFileType)`; MainActivity no longer resolves note bodies or touches body files at all. B2-UI-1 lock semantics (defer, never drop, no plaintext) + B1-AUTH-05 imports-root confinement retained. Tests: new `B2Ui5MarkdownSaveSerializationTest` (13 — latest-wins supersede, a slow older write can never land after a newer one, in-flight serialization, a 24-way torn-write simulator leaves only a complete body + the last-issued body, a reader awaiting settle sees the committed value + chases a newer request issued while waiting, bounded-settle timing seam, per-page independence, + wiring source pins). `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` 1386 total (1383 green; the only failures are the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` asserts on `docs/RELEASE.md`/`app/build.gradle.kts` + the documented `WikiLinkParserCacheUnitTest` cancellation flake — all three proven pre-existing by failing identically on a stashed clean tree) + `gradle assembleDebug` green (debug APK 173,751,590 bytes). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-75 | `DONE` | B2-DEPS-03 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-75/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DEPS-03 row). Repo-local Gradle dependency verification is ON: `gradle/verification-metadata.xml` is committed — 519 components / 913 sha256-pinned artifacts covering `com.android.tools.build` (AGP, aapt2 incl. the `aapt2-*-linux.jar` platform classifier, lint), `org.jetbrains.kotlin` (Kotlin + compose compiler) and `com.google.devtools.ksp`, i.e. the build plugins named in the finding. Gradle 8.13 auto-enables STRICT checksum verification for EVERY resolved artifact (project deps, POM/module metadata, AND plugins) the moment that file is present — a compromised/MITM'd/poisoned-cache artifact now fails the build loudly instead of compiling into the signed APK. Bootstrap followed the documented incremental flow: `--write-verification-metadata sha256 help` then the REAL task set (`testDebugUnitTest assembleDebug`) so task-execution-time resolutions (platform-suffixed aapt2, lint/uast/play-sdk-proto) are pinned; round-trip proven by `gradle assembleDebug` passing with NO write flag (the pre-bootstrap run failed with `Dependency verification failed … aapt2 … checksum is missing from verification metadata`). `settings.gradle.kts` `dependencyResolutionManagement` (`:17-28`) mirrors the `pluginManagement` google() content filters so a polluted google index can never publish a fake org.jetbrains/io.coil-kt artifact; `mavenCentral()` retained. The attempt's `dependencyVerification { verify = "all" }` settings block — a Gradle-8.13 non-entity that broke settings compilation (`Unresolved reference: dependencyVerification`, proven in a minimal repro + bytecode scan of the distribution, which ships no such settings accessor) — was REMOVED; verification is file-driven, no settings DSL exists. Tests: new `B2Deps03DependencyVerificationTest` (5 — mirror filters, mavenCentral retained, broken DSL absent, metadata present + real, build-plugin groups pinned). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1391 total (only the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` asserts; inputs untouched) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched (CI `distributionSha256Sum` + pinned opencode-install stay external notes — workflow edits prohibited). |
| phase-76 | `DONE` | B2-DEPS-04 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-76/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DEPS-04 row). The downloadable-plugin signing identity is no longer a public default or an ephemeral build-bred keystore: `plugins/llm/build.gradle.kts` no longer hardcodes a default signing password and no longer runs the JDK keystore-generation CLI to mint a fresh self-signed JKS every build. The signing tasks (`:plugins:llm:signPlugin`/`verifyPluginSignature`/`pluginMetadata`) now FAIL LOUDLY — a `gradle.taskGraph.whenReady` gate (mirroring the `:app` phase-57 release gate) plus `requirePluginSigningKeystoreB64()`/`requirePluginSigningStorePass()` throw a `GradleException` when `PLUGIN_SIGNING_KEYSTORE_B64`/`PLUGIN_SIGNING_STORE_PASS` are unset (`PLUGIN_SIGNING_KEY_PASS` optional, defaults to the store password, never a committed constant). The dangling `:app:generateLlmPluginSeed` claim became a REAL task in `app/build.gradle.kts`: it depends on `:plugins:llm:pluginMetadata` (which fails without the signing env), validates the signed artifact's `sha256` (64-hex) + `pinnedCertHash` (`sha256/<base64>`), and rewrites the committed `GeneratedLlmPluginPin.kt` seed (`null` = fail-closed, no release pinned yet). `CompileTimePluginPins.RELEASES` now folds that seed in via `buildReleaseTable(*listOfNotNull(llmPluginSeedRelease).toTypedArray())`. A latent pre-existing bug (`dependsOn(pluginSigningKeystore)` passed a `Provider<RegularFile>` as a task dependency, so `signPlugin` could never run even with a keystore) was fixed. Positive path proven with a THROWAWAY `/tmp` keystore: seed task emitted the exact pin of the key that signed the artifact, then the pin was reverted (never committed). Tests: new `B2Deps04PluginSigningTest` (9 — source-pin + repo-scan, needle literals runtime-composed so the guard file can't trip itself). `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` 1456 green (0 failures/errors; the documented `WikiLinkParserCacheUnitTest` flake passed in isolation)