| phase-78 | `DONE` | B2-DOS-02 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-78/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DOS-02 row). Vault search is bounded at every layer: new pure-JVM `services/VaultSearchPolicy.kt` owns the budgets (`SEARCH_CORPUS_CAP = 1500`, `DEEP_SCAN_BATCH_SIZE = 1500`, `exceedsCorpusCap`/`cachedWindowSize`/`isBlankQuery`/`pageMatches`/`refineNoticeMessage`). `NoteRepository.loadSearchCorpus` (`NoteRepository.kt:107-126`) now ALWAYS caches the decrypted window via the bounded DAO read `getAllActivePagesBounded` (`Daos.kt`, `LIMIT :limit`) — a keystroke search never re-decrypts the vault (pre-fix the >1500 vault dropped the cache, so every keystroke re-ran a full-vault AES-GCM); over-cap vaults are flagged via `NoteRepository.searchCorpusCapped` (recomputed per load). `searchPages` filters the cached window only; the EXPLICIT user-approved refine path is `deepSearchPages` (`:412-434`), paged via `getAllActivePagesPaged` (`LIMIT :limit OFFSET :offset`, only matches retained, cancellable). `NoteflowViewModel.searchVault` shares ONE cancellable `Job` (`searchVaultJob?.cancel()` before every launch + `if (isActive)` guard, `:1926-1934`) and `deepSearchVault` (`:1942-1948`) shares it, so concurrent keystrokes pre-empt in-flight decrypts. `HomeScreen` shows a one-time non-alarming "Search covers the most recent pages" banner + "Search all pages" action (`HomeScreen.kt`, gated on `viewModel.repository.searchCorpusCapped` + `refinedSearchDone`). Command palette indexes the same bounded window. Tests: `B2Dos02VaultSearchBoundedTest` (10 — policy decision table + wiring source pins). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |

| phase-79 | `DONE` | B2-DOS-03 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-79/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DOS-03 row). Voice-note recording is bounded and the amplitude sampler is off-main. New pure-JVM `services/VoiceRecordingPolicy.kt` (decision table: `MAX_RECORDING_DURATION_MS` = 30 min, `MAX_RECORDING_BYTES` = 32 MB, `SAMPLER_TICK_MS` = 100, `MAX_STORED_WAVEFORM_ENTRIES` = 600, non-alarming limit messages) + `services/LiveWaveformBuckets.kt` (preallocated `FloatArray` accumulator; O(1)-amortized `append`; fold-on-full so `snapshot()` never exceeds `WaveformPeakMath.recordingLiveBuckets` = 160 and stays mean-preserving across the whole session). `VoiceNoteManager` sampler now runs on `Dispatchers.Default` (`VoiceNoteManager.kt:150`), appends `waveformBuckets.append(...)` and emits `waveformBuckets.snapshot()` (`:158`) — the pre-fix `_waveformAmplitudes.value + amp` full-list copy-on-write per 100 ms tick (~648M element copies after 1 h) on the main thread is gone — and aborts at the duration/file-size ceilings via `finalizeRecording(limitMessage)` (`:160-175`), which stops+encrypts (B1-DB-3 path preserved), surfaces a non-alarming `recordingError`, and publishes `completedRecordingResult` so `EditorScreen`'s `LaunchedEffect(completedVoiceRecording)` auto-attaches the audio embed through the shared `attachVoiceRecording` helper (never discarded, never orphaned). `startRecording`/`stopRecording`/`finalizeRecording` are serialized under a new `recorderLock` (`VoiceNoteManager.kt:75`) so a chip-tap stop racing a sampler ceiling-abort can never double-finalize. `NoteRepository.parseWaveformJson` (`:997-1009`) is bounded to 600 entries (both JSONArray + fallback paths). Tests: `LiveWaveformBucketsTest` (9) + `VoiceRecordingPolicyTest` (6) + `B2Dos03VoiceRecordingTest` (12, wiring source pins). `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest` 1429 total (only the 2 pre-existing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` asserts on untouched `app/build.gradle.kts`/`docs/RELEASE.md`, pre-existing since phase-55) + `gradle :app:assembleDebug` green (APK SHA-256 `5cc83e79…`). No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. |
| phase-80 | `DONE` | B2-DOS-04 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-80/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DOS-04 row). `AppFacadeHost.httpGet` enforces the 10 MB response cap DURING the read, never after `readBytes()` already slurped the entire body into heap (the pre-fix `contentLengthLong` pre-check is -1/skipped for chunked/unknown responses, so a granted plugin pointing at a slow-chunked endpoint could pin hundreds of MB and OOM the process; the whole body arrived in heap BEFORE the `bytes.size > MAX` comparison). New pure-JVM `services/FacadeHttpGetPolicy.kt` is the single decision table (`MAX_FACADE_GET_BYTES` = 10 MB, `READ_BUFFER_BYTES` = 64 KiB): `readCapped` mirrors `WebPageFetcher` — a bounded streaming loop that throws `ResponseTooLargeException` mid-stream on the first chunk crossing the cap, so the heap accumulator can never exceed the budget + one read buffer. `AppFacadeHost.httpGet` (`AppFacadeHost.kt:91-93`) routes every body read through `FacadeHttpGetPolicy.readCapped`; the dead `readBytes()`-size post-check and the private `MAX_FACADE_GET_BYTES` companion are deleted; the `contentLengthLong` header pre-check (`:82-85`) stays as an early exit and the B1-NET-05 manual-redirect posture (`instanceFollowRedirects = false` `:67`, per-hop `StrictRedirectPolicy` re-validation `:71-76`) is retained so every redirect hop carries its OWN 10 MB budget. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched. API 26+ floor, pure java.io (no newer-API requirement, no fallback needed). Tests: new `B2Dos04FacadeGetStreamingCapTest` (7 — slow-chunked over-cap abort proven via a synthetic drip stream that never fully drains + bounded-yield assertion, exactly-at-cap accepted, small-body round-trip, header pre-check refuses before the stream opens, per-hop budget on a redirect chain, + source pins for readBytes-removal / readCapped-wiring / policy loop). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1436 total green (0 failures — the previously-failing `B1Plat01ReleaseSigningTest` asserts were repaired by the `b9a0b52` CI fix) + `gradle :app:assembleDebug` green (APK 173,760,926 bytes, SHA-256 `bc94479c…`). |
| phase-81 | `DONE` | B2-DOS-05 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-81/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DOS-05 row). Attachment/import ingestion is bounded DURING the read, never post-slurp — a 500 MB picker/PDF/zip can no longer be `readBytes()`-ed wholly into heap to OOM the process (reachable via exported `ACTION_SEND */*` B1-PLAT-2 or any picker; repeatable as DoS). New pure-JVM decision table `services/AttachmentIngestPolicy.kt`: `MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES` = 25 MB, `READ_BUFFER_BYTES` = 64 KiB; `boundedReadBytes` streams over a fixed buffer and throws `ImportArchivePolicy.ImportSizeLimitException` mid-stream on the first chunk crossing the cap (heap never exceeds budget + one buffer); `readTextHead` is a head-bounded, prefix-preserving UTF-8 text head read (a multi-byte char split at the cap decodes lossily to a single replacement char, never an over-read past the budget; empty for missing/unreadable/empty). `EditorScreen` all 3 picker sites (`:236` custom-bg, `:263` paper-texture, `:829` photo embed) route through `boundedReadBytes` with a dedicated size-limit catch per site → truthful non-alarming snackbar ("Background image / Paper texture / Photo ... too large (max 25 MB)"), never silent; the pre-existing texture-path `inputStream?.close()` leak was removed (now `use`). `NoteflowViewModel.restoreEncryptedBackupFromZip` (`:3145-3147`) replaced `sourceZip.readBytes()` with `boundedReadBytes(it, ImportExportService.MAX_BACKUP_INPUT_BYTES)` — the 400 MB restore budget is preserved but enforced in-flight. `DocumentTextExtractor` rewritten: `MAX_EXTRACT_BYTES` = 25 MB (PDF operator scan head) + `MAX_TEXT_HEAD_BYTES` = 1 MB (text head, preserving the old `< 1_000_000` guard's spirit); `text` branch → `readTextBounded`, `extractPdfText` → `readFirstBytesBounded(file, MAX_EXTRACT_BYTES)`; no `file.readBytes()`/`file.readText()` left. Legacy plaintext-file-body reads switched to `AttachmentIngestPolicy.readTextHead` in `NoteBodyVaultPolicy.kt:64` and `WikiLinkParser.kt:274`. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, API-26+ pure java.io. Tests: new `B2Dos05AttachmentIngestTest` (14 — behavior via a synthetic `DripInputStream` proving mid-stream abort with bounded yield (never drains, never exceeds budget + buffer), exactly-at-cap accepted, small round-trip, empty stream, head-head read of a 1 MB file under a 64 KiB budget returns only a budget-length PREFIX (bounded + prefix-preserving), zero/missing-file degenerate cases, PDF-operator head found inside a giant PDF, + source pins: EditorScreen exactly 3 `boundedReadBytes` references with no raw `.readBytes()` after `openInputStream`, NoteflowViewModel no `sourceZip.readBytes()` + bounded read with backup budget, DocumentTextExtractor no raw readBytes/readText and uses `readFirstBytesBounded`, NoteBodyVaultPolicy/WikiLinkParser use `readTextHead`). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1470 total green (0 failures) + `gradle :app:assembleDebug` green. **Phase-81 review fixes** (same lineage): `NoteRepository.migrateLegacyPlaintextNoteBodies` (`:515`) — the last wholesale `file.readText()` on the legacy-body surface — now refuses oversized (> 25 MB) bodies (never read/deleted) and reads within-cap bodies head-bounded; WebDAV restore over-budget archives fail CLOSED with a truthful "Backup is too large to restore (max 400 MB)" message; `resolveBodyForDisplay` never returns a truncated head for oversized legacy bodies (falls through to the full column); `EditorScreen`'s 3 picker reads moved off the main thread; `boundedReadBytes` guards a contract-breaking zero-progress stream (throws after 16 idle reads). `B2Dos05AttachmentIngestTest` now 15 tests, 1471 total green + `assembleDebug` green. |
| phase-82 | `DONE` | B2-DOS-06 (MEDIUM) fixed (see `workspace/phase-82/REPORT.md` + `docs/security-report.md` B2-DOS-06 row). Multi-layer PSD export no longer materializes N full-page ARGB bitmaps + N per-layer channel buffers at once — a ~25-layer note export dropped from ~350 MB peak heap to a bounded ~125-132 MB, on every export. New pure-JVM decision table `services/PsdExportPolicy.kt`: `MAX_EXPORT_LAYER_COUNT` = 16, `capLayerCount`/`omittedLayerCount`/`isLayerCountCapped` (the layer-budget arithmetic) + `noticeMessage` (the one-time non-alarming wording, says which end of the stack was kept). `ImportExportService.exportPageToPsd` (`:2422`) clamps before rendering: it keeps the TOP 16 DATA layers of `layers.sortedBy { it.zOrder }` (highest zOrder = the visually front-most, most recently worked-on layers) in bottom→top PSD record order via `takeLast(exportedDataLayers)`/`dropLast(exportedDataLayers)` (the old unbounded `sortedBy { it.zOrder }.forEachIndexed` bitmap-every-layer loop is gone; a restored crafted vault can no longer raise the bitmap count), folds the omitted BOTTOM layers into ONE bounded merged-preview bitmap (`compositeExtras`) so the PSD's flattened composite still shows the full page, and returns the new `PsdExportService.PsdExportOutcome(file, exportedLayerCount, omittedLayerCount)`; `EditorScreen.kt:1407-1420` shows "PSD export included the top N of M layers — K omitted (max 16)" via `PsdExportPolicy.noticeMessage` AFTER a successful export (a cancelled picker can no longer hide the omission behind "Export cancelled"; never silent degradation). `PsdExportService.exportLayersToPsd` now writes the layer-and-mask section STREAMING: the info records go into a tiny bounded buffer (`layerRecordBytes`, few KB for 16 layers), the per-layer channel PIXEL data is written straight to the destination `DataOutputStream` one channel at a time (`writeLayerChannelData` → `writeChannelPixels`) — the pre-fix `layerPixelBlocks` full-size per-layer channel `ByteArray` accumulation AND the per-layer `IntArray(width*height)` are gone — and ONE `IntArray(width*height)` is reused for every layer and the composite, with a defensive `take(MAX_EXPORT_LAYER_COUNT + 1)` clamp plus a bounded `compositeExtras.take(MAX_EXPORT_LAYER_COUNT)` composite pass. The section-length arithmetic (`channelSizeFor`/`channelDataLength`/`layerSectionLength`) keeps the PSD layout byte-identical to the pre-fix materialized section. No schema change, no migration, no new deps, `.github/workflows/` untouched, API-26+ (pure JVM; the psd layout helpers are unit-testable without Android). Tests: new `B2Dos06PsdExportLayerCapTest` (16 — policy behavior incl. cap/clamp/omission/notice, the streaming writer's channel-size/section-length/layer-record byte layout, single-pixel-buffer reuse, hidden-layer flag, dedup + source pins: no `layerPixelBlocks`/`chanBos`, exactly one `IntArray(width * height)`, ImportExportService uses `PsdExportPolicy.capLayerCount` + `takeLast(exportedDataLayers)` + returns `PsdExportOutcome`, EditorScreen surfaces `PsdExportPolicy.noticeMessage`, merged-preview `compositeExtras` folding + `MAX_EXPORT_LAYER_COUNT + 1` defensive clamp pins). `gradle testDebugUnitTest` 1487 total green (0 failures) + `gradle assembleDebug` green. |

